   "html_text": "As the previous examples show, explanatory proofs could be of several types and explain in different manners. A recent debate has focused on the issue of whether proofs by induction are explanatory. On the one hand, Lange (2010) argues that proofs by induction are not explanatory. His argument relies on the use of a form of upward and downward induction from a fixed number k, with k≠1. According to Lange, if proofs by ordinary mathematical induction are explanatory, so are proofs by upward and d",
